From 498b2c234faa110f637fbe39469367b4c3127305 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 16:05:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] set_membership pass: fold ==-chains into BitTest
 clusters; fix TWO redundant_ext miscompiles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

NEW PASS (OP-15 wiring for IS-06): src/passes/set_membership.rs folds
CondBranch chains of 'x==C1 || x==C2 || ...' (>= 3 members, the
post-range_fold/cfg_simplify shape: hit edges straight into one join
Phi, optional value-block tail) into GCC's classify idiom:
sub lo; unsigned range guard; BitTest MASK; and. Members may be Eq
tests OR range_fold products (contiguous bit runs), span <= 63,
32-bit mask/BT when span <= 31. Fail-closed guards: single-pred
chain interior, block-local defs (tail Cmp: exactly the one Phi use),
zext-only domains (signed narrow roots excluded), overlap-checked
Phi edge retargeting; absorbed blocks die in cfg_simplify's
unreachable sweep. Runs right after range_fold. 7 unit tests.
Kill switch: CCC_DISABLE_PASSES=set_membership.
xml_name_continue now emits two bt clusters (like GCC); expat_xml_scan
1.90x -> 1.86x; exhaustive 0..255 hash matches gcc at -O0..-Os.

MISCOMPILE FIX 1 (found running the new pass's validation): the
always-on redundant_ext removed 'movzbl %al,%eax' whenever
upper32_zero — but that only proves bits 32..63. After the movq->movl
narrowing, 'movl %edi,%eax; movzbl %al,%eax' lost the movzbl and
f(unsigned char c){return c>=0xc2U;} returned bits 8..31 of the
argument (O1: f(191)==1). A byte re-extension needs is_byte (bits
8..31 zero); the 64-bit form additionally upper32_zero. Same
hardening applied to the movzwl/movzwq 16-bit twin.

MISCOMPILE FIX 2 (fuzz seeds 4/9/100, pre-existing at -O2): the
movq->movl copy narrowing's only gate was 'next instruction consumes
the 32-bit destination form' — a 32-bit READ does not end a 64-bit
live range. Seed 4: 'movq %rax,%r15' narrowed because the next line
read %r15d, but 'movq %r15,%rcx' consumed the full hash 60 lines
later. The narrowing now requires the SOURCE to be provably
upper-32-zero (identity transform); the next-use check remains as a
profitability filter. Both always-on passes gained bisection gates
(CCC_NO_REDUNDANT_EXT / CCC_NO_PUSHF_ELIM).

Validation: x86-64 differential fuzz 300/300 at O1+O2 (was 147/150 —
seeds 4/9/100 now FIXED), m32 fuzz 200/200, 998/998 unit, 50/50
correctness, 46/46 checks, regparm all levels, -m32 benchmark parity
(nbody, spectral_norm, binary_trees, struct_copy).
