32-bit targets only <= 32-bit BitTests; i128 excluded everywhere.
set_membership's mask width is likewise capped at span<=31 for -m32.

BUG FIX 2 (i686 miscompile): the accumulator BitTest arm hardcoded
'btl %ecx,%eax' — but the shared rhs staging uses the index's REGISTER
HOME when it has one, leaving %ecx stale (set_membership at -m32
classified '/' as an XML name char). The BT now uses rhs_ref exactly
like every other ALU op in that match.

