From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:12:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] set_membership v2: skip-tolerant clustering, ASCII
 case-fold merge, best-window selection, head-prelude tolerance

Four structural upgrades, closing the gap to GCC's classify codegen
(xml_name_continue: 45 pre-pass -> 42 -> 28 instructions; GCC 20):

1. SKIP-TOLERANT COLLECTION: any pure single-compare test that is not
   maskable (Expat's 'c >= 0xc2U' mid-chain) becomes a Skip member.
   ||-commutativity over pure tests lets mask members collect ACROSS
   skips into ONE cluster (was: the skip split the set into two
   sub-threshold halves and nothing folded). Survivors are re-chained
   behind the cluster; when the value-carrying tail is absorbed, the
   last surviving test converts into the new tail (its 0/1 condition
   feeds the Phi directly).

2. ASCII CASE-FOLD MERGE (GCC's andl $-33): two Range members [a,b]
   and [a+32,b+32] with bit 5 clear across [a,b] merge into one test
   on x & ~32. Exact for all inputs: clearing bit 5 maps the upper
   range onto the lower and nothing else into it. a-z/A-Z now costs
   one and+sub+cmp instead of two sub+cmp chains.

3. BEST-WINDOW SELECTION: instead of requiring ALL members within one
   span, pick the width-limited window (63/31 by target) containing
   the most maskable members; outliers survive as ordinary tests
   (test: {0,5,9,200} keeps 200 as the converted tail).

4. HEAD-PRELUDE TOLERANCE: the chain head often carries the function
   entry (Alloca/ParamRef/zext) before its test. The test is parsed
   as a block SUFFIX; prelude instructions are preserved verbatim by
   both rewrites, and the defs-local check skips them (they are not
   deleted, so external uses are legal).

Each transform fires once per call and returns (edges/labels go stale);
the driver fixpoint iterates. New in-crate IR INTERPRETER for the tests
drives exhaustive 0..255 equivalence of the full folded Expat chain
against the C semantics, plus shape tests for case-fold bit-5
legality, skip-crossing, window outliers, and all prior guards (8 unit
tests).

Validation: 999/999 unit, 50/50 correctness, 46/46 checks, x64 fuzz
300/300, m32 fuzz 200/200, regparm all levels, exhaustive classify
parity -m64/-m32, nbody -O0 exact.
